  "result": "Done! I've implemented customer merging functionality. Here's what was added:\n\n**Added to src/customers.js:**\n- `mergeCustomers(customers, invoices, fromId, intoId)` \u2014 merges duplicate customers\n  - **Removes** fromId customer from the customers array\n  - **Reassigns** all invoices belonging to fromId to intoId\n  - Returns `ok({ customers, invoices })` with merged arrays\n  - **Normalizes IDs** before processing (case-insensitive, whitespace-trimmed)\n  - **Never mutates** input arrays\n  - **Preserves** invoice properties, payments, and order\n  - **Errors:**\n    - SAME_CUSTOMER: if fromId and intoId are the same\n    - CUSTOMER_NOT_FOUND: if either customer doesn't exist\n\n**Added to src/errors.js:**\n- SAME_CUSTOMER error code\n\n**Created test/merge-customers.test.js:**\n- 16 comprehensive test cases covering:\n  - Successful merge of invoices from one customer to another\n  - Same customer rejection\n  - Unknown customer rejection\n  - Normalized ID handling (case-insensitive, whitespace-trimmed)\n  - Non-mutation of input arrays\n  - Empty invoices array\n  - Multiple invoices from from-customer\n  - Preservation of other customers' invoices\n  - Draft and partially paid invoices with payments preserved\n  - Customer properties preservation\n  - Order preservation (customers and invoices)\n  - Case-insensitive ID matching\n\n**Results:**\n- All 295 tests passing (16 new merge tests + 33 currency + 21 CSV + 10 late fee + 15 VAT + 16 overdue + 184 existing)\n- Customer data deduplication capability\n- Clean merge preserving all invoice history",
